<configuration name="xml_curl.conf" description="cURL XML Gateway">
  <!--
    The user directory, fetched from the API instead of read from disk.

    ── Why ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    The directory used to be twenty files under conf/directory/default/, 1000
    through 1019, each carrying `$${default_password}` — one password shared by
    every agent on the platform, and a hard ceiling of twenty SIP identities.
    Two agencies were handed the same extension, so whichever browser
    registered last received both agencies' calls, and any agent could register
    as any extension because they all authenticated with the same secret.

    Each agent now has a row in `agent_sip_credentials` with an extension that
    is unique across the platform and a password that is theirs alone. This
    binding is how FreeSWITCH reads it. See apps/api/src/routes/freeswitch-directory.ts.

    ── The static files still work ───────────────────────────────────────────

    When the endpoint answers `<result status="not found"/>` FreeSWITCH falls
    through to the next binding for the section, which is the XML still on
    disk. So vapi.xml, demo-agent.xml and every 1000..1019 file resolve exactly
    as they did, and agents move onto database credentials one at a time rather
    than in a single cutover. Deleting those files is a later step, once no
    registration depends on them.

    ── The URL and the key ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

    `http://api:3001` is the in-cluster address the dialplan's carrier-route
    lookup already uses, so this reaches the API the same proven way.

    The shared secret travels as `?k=` because mod_curl cannot set a request
    header — the same constraint, and the same trade-off, recorded in
    apps/api/src/lib/internal-auth.ts and in the vars.xml comment above
    `internal_key`. FreeSWITCH logs the URLs it fetches, so this key is its own
    secret, used for nothing but these callbacks, and cheap to rotate.
  -->
  <bindings>
    <binding name="directory">
      <param name="gateway-url" value="http://api:3001/api/v1/freeswitch/directory?k=$${internal_key}" bindings="directory"/>
      <param name="method" value="post"/>
      <!--
        A registration waits on this fetch, so the timeout is what an agent
        experiences when the API is slow. Four seconds is long enough for a
        database round trip on a cold connection and short enough that a hung
        API fails the registration rather than hanging the SIP transaction —
        at which point the static XML is consulted and a legacy extension
        still comes up.
      -->
      <param name="timeout" value="4"/>
      <param name="connect-timeout" value="2"/>
      <!--
        Without this, libcurl sends `Expect: 100-continue` on the POST and waits
        for an interim response that Fastify does not send, adding a one-second
        stall to every directory lookup — which is every registration and every
        call to an agent.
      -->
      <param name="disable-100-continue" value="true"/>
    </binding>
  </bindings>
</configuration>
